      "ambientText": "Rain on the hut roof. Machines idling. Nobody here speaks to the visitor.",
      "clues": [
        {
          "label": "The bombe's plugboard",
          "detail": "Routed wires and a rotating drum, built to search a space no human could hold in their head. It was described, generously, as a machine that could not think.",
          "x": 0.62,
          "y": 0.58,
          "figureQuote": "He gave me this; I think of him when I see it. Britain was his office before it was mine.",
          "index": 1,
          "sceneIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "A portrait of the staff roll",
          "detail": "Dozens of faces outside this hut, credited in a register that never appeared in the official history. One name among them reads: that is all I am permitted to say.",
          "x": 0.35,
          "y": 0.48,
          "figureQuote": "He sat for this portrait when Britain was theirs. I learned the room before I learned the work.",
          "index": 2,
          "sceneIndex": 1
        }
      ],
